#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Heightmap and biome reference data from worlds generated by vanilla servers.

For every world of the worlds file this starts a local vanilla dedicated
server (127.0.0.1 only, no rcon/query) with the requested world type,
generates the listed areas to full chunks, saves, and writes the stored
WORLD_SURFACE / OCEAN_FLOOR heightmaps and the stored chunk biomes to
data/<level_type>_<mc>_<seed>.txt. Format and conventions: README.md.

Usage:
  worldgen_reference.py --mc 1.21.1 --level-type amplified \
      --worlds worlds.txt --work <scratch dir>
  worldgen_reference.py --mc 1.21.1 --datapack testpack --work <scratch dir>

With --datapack the pack (a folder or a zip) is put into the world's datapacks
folder before the server creates the world, so a pack that replaces
minecraft:overworld defines the generator. Files are then named
data/<pack name>_<mc>_<seed>.txt.
"""

